 <rationallyprime@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 00:10:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] REPA: Z-Image target tokens

Implements the two REPA hooks for Z-Image: latents are cut into 2x2 patches,
one token each, and the main `layers` stack sees the image tokens first
(padded to a multiple of 32), then the caption, so the target image is the
first h * w tokens.

The pixel-space ZImageL2PModel inherits from ZImageModel and uses 16 px
patches, so it opts out explicitly instead of inheriting a wrong layout.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 README.md                                             |  2 +-
 .../diffusion_models/z_image/z_image.py               | 11 +++++++++++
 .../diffusion_models/z_image/z_image_l2p_model.py     |  4 ++++
 3 files changed, 16 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index c91db97..803dc04 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -387,7 +387,7 @@ It is off unless the process config has a `repa` block, next to `train`, `model`
       projector_dim: 2048              # hidden width of the mlp projector
 ```
 
-Supported models: Qwen-Image-2.1. The values above are SimpleTuner's Qwen-Image-2.1 preset (DINOv2 ViT-g/14,
+Supported models: Qwen-Image-2.1 and Z-Image. The values above are SimpleTuner's Qwen-Image-2.1 preset (DINOv2 ViT-g/14,
 block 8, lambda 0.5) with the paper's projector. Other models are added with two methods on their model class
 (`get_repa_token_grid` and `get_repa_target_tokens` in `toolkit/models/base_model.py`) and a
 `get_transformer_block_names` entry. A model without them fails at setup with a message saying so.
diff --git a/extensions_built_in/diffusion_models/z_image/z_image.py b/extensions_built_in/diffusion_models/z_image/z_image.py
index fed40e0..5cb1177 100644
--- a/extensions_built_in/diffusion_models/z_image/z_image.py
+++ b/extensions_built_in/diffusion_models/z_image/z_image.py
@@ -393,5 +393,16 @@ class ZImageModel(BaseModel):
     def get_transformer_block_names(self) -> Optional[List[str]]:
         return ["layers"]
 
+    def get_repa_token_grid(self, latent_height: int, latent_width: int):
+        # the latents are cut into 2x2 patches, one token each
+        return latent_height // 2, latent_width // 2
+
+    def get_repa_target_tokens(self, block_output, latents: torch.Tensor) -> torch.Tensor:
+        # the image tokens come first in the sequence (padded to a multiple of 32), then the
+        # caption, and the tokens are row-major, so the target image is the first h * w
+        height, width = self.get_repa_token_grid(*latents.shape[-2:])
+        hidden = block_output[0] if isinstance(block_output, (tuple, list)) else block_output
+        return hidden[:, : height * width].reshape(latents.shape[0], height, width, -1)
+
     lora_keys_use_comfy_prefix = True
 
diff --git a/extensions_built_in/diffusion_models/z_image/z_image_l2p_model.py b/extensions_built_in/diffusion_models/z_image/z_image_l2p_model.py
index b642935..6271e1e 100644
--- a/extensions_built_in/diffusion_models/z_image/z_image_l2p_model.py
+++ b/extensions_built_in/diffusion_models/z_image/z_image_l2p_model.py
@@ -288,6 +288,10 @@ class ZImageTransformer2DModel(ZImageTransformer2DModelOriginal):
 class ZImageL2PModel(ZImageModel):
     arch = "zimage_l2p"
 
+    def get_repa_token_grid(self, latent_height: int, latent_width: int):
+        # a pixel-space variant with 16 px patches: ZImageModel's layout does not apply
+        return None
+
     def load_model(self):
         dtype = self.torch_dtype
         self.print_and_status_update("Loading ZImage model")
